## `#process()` method

The core traversal loop wraps each root traversal in a try/catch:

```js
for (const root of roots) {
    try {
        this.#traverse(root, effects, render_effects);
    } catch (e) {
        reset_all(root);
        if (!this.#is_deferred()) this.discard();
        throw e;
    }
}
```

When an error is thrown during traversal, it calls `reset_all(root)` to mark the whole tree clean. The comment explains that if no async work remains, the branch is dead and must be discarded to avoid becoming a "zombie" — the discard only happens when `!this.#is_deferred()`, then the error is re-thrown.

The `reset_all` helper recursively sets `CLEAN` status on the effect and its children.

Notably, `#process()` sets `current_batch = null` after roots are handled ("any writes should take effect in a subsequent batch"), and there's `async_mode_flag` handling around committing:

```js
if (async_mode_flag) {
    this.#commit();
    current_batch = next_batch;
